{"title":"Subjectwise Test-12 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 CS Discrete Mathematics","fileName":"032_Subjectwise Test-12 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 CS Discrete Mathematics.html","branch":"COMPUTER SCIENCE ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 GATE 2025 Online Test Series Computer Science Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":5400,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>In a finite directed graph, every vertex has exactly three incoming edges. Which of the following statements is guaranteed to be true?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Some vertex has at least three edges leaving it.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Exactly three edges leave every vertex.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Some vertex has exactly three edges leaving it.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of the above is true.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/666f22fef03131982f6ecf6e671e55febeed1b1a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Let <em>X</em> be a set of size n. What is the size of the set <img src=\"/media/faa2953a0ed2025bdd3a6c3f9cfede03170843d6.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/3ba26c134b27310aa12642567f9c892f2c9b4341.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/85256ddd94a8e5bc8c6fc82834a5e7fe2a95460e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/bf909a38e6d7e3cf3dbfc6b17d79e6306ae76596.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/c383d0c96d9eface0f0324c7366e7da18ad70b5d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </d